   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">Hi,</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">I have been using the CamtrapR package for\r\npreparing the data for spatial capture-recapture models.</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">In my dataset, I have multiple\r\npictures with more than one dingo identified. If for example, a picture\r\ncontains dingo A and dingo B, I would expect that the Record Table should\r\ninclude a line for both dingoes, unless these dingoes were found in another\r\npicture less than the minDeltaTime specified. However, I have realised that</span> the\r\nresulting Record Table would only take into consideration the first individual\r\nrecorded (Dingo A) in the ‘HierarchicalSubject’ of the metadata of each picture\r\nand not the subsequent identified individuals (Dingo B, C, etc).<span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">Here is the code I have been\r\nusing:</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#006fc9\">recordTableIndividualDingo\r\n&lt;- recordTableIndividual(inDir  = wd_images_ID_dingoes,</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 72pt;text-indent:36pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#006fc9\">IDfrom                 =\r\n&quot;metadata&quot;,</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 72pt;text-indent:36pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#006fc9\">hasStationFolders      =\r\nFALSE,         # images are not in\r\nstation directories</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 72pt;text-indent:36pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#006fc9\">metadataIDTag          =\r\n&quot;Individual_dingo&quot;,</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 72pt;text-indent:36pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#006fc9\">additionalMetadataTags\r\n=  c(&quot;EXIF:AmbientTemperature&quot;,\r\n&quot;UserLabel&quot;,  &quot;EXIF:Model&quot;), </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 72pt;text-indent:36pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#006fc9\">minDeltaTime           =\r\n10,</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 72pt;text-indent:36pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#006fc9\">deltaTimeComparedTo    =\r\n&quot;lastIndependentRecord&quot;,</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 72pt;text-indent:36pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:#006fc9\">metadataHierarchyDelimitor\r\n= &quot;|&quot;)</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">A quick way that I found to\r\nwork around this problem was to add the argument ‘</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#006fc9\">removeDuplicateRecords = FALS</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">E’ in the function recordTableIndividual.</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">The resulting table seems to\r\ninclude all individuals in the pictures (e.g. Dingo A AND Dingo B). I would\r\nthen remove the ‘real’ duplicates from the table (that is the lines containing\r\nthe same individual during the exact same time) as so:</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:#006fc9\">recordTableIndividual_final\r\n&lt;-recordTableIndividual[!duplicated(recordTableIndividual[,c(&quot;Individual&quot;,&quot;DateTimeOriginal&quot;)]),]</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">This approach seems to give the\r\ncorrect results in the table.</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">If needed, I can share a subsample\r\nof the data extracted with exiftool. In the hierarchicalsubject column, we can\r\nfind, for example: <u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">Individual_dingo|DingoA,\r\nIndividual_dingo|DingoB, SPECIES|Dog</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">I was wondering if anybody had\r\nany comments or suggestions about this specific situation.</span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></p><p style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Calibri,Helvetica,sans-serif,serif,EmojiFont;font-size:16px;line-height:normal\">\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">Thank you very much in advance\r\nfor your help,</span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\"><br></span></p><p style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;color:black\">Vanessa</span></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "QAKy8rMUBwAJ",
   "from": "Juergen Niedballa",
   "author": "0b86ca0cb4b615b0",
   "date": "2019-03-06T14:12:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: RecordTableIndividual CamtrapR question",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Vanessa,<div>thank you for the question. There is indeed a bug in the current code of <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">recordTableIndividual</font>. </div><div><br></div><div>As you described, the problem is this: if there are 2 or more individuals at the same station at the same time (i.e., you tagged different individuals in the same picture), and <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">removeDuplicateRecords = TRUE</font>, only one record will be returned (the first one) and the rest omitted. This may happen with both methods for individual ID: metadata tags and directories for individuals.</div><div><br></div><div>Please find attached 2 R scripts in which the problem should be fixed. They contain an updated version of recordTableIndividual and some helper functions needed by recordTableIndividual internally. </div><div><br></div><div>Can you please run/source both scripts (no need to change anything inside) and then rerun your recordTableIndividual code? Then <b>please</b>, let us know if it worked. If so, it will be part of the next camtrapR release.</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you very much for reporting. </div><div>Best,</div><div>Jürgen</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "vCfIL8JaBwAJ",
   "from": "Vanessa Gabriele",
   "author": "36a47ebce6e417b3",
   "date": "2019-03-07T11:35:59Z",
   "subject": "Re: RecordTableIndividual CamtrapR question",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Jürgen;<div><br></div><div>Thanks for your response. I did run the new function, and the resulting table seems to be identical to the one I would obtain with the &#39;alternative&#39; approach that I was using. So, it seems to work! </div><div><br></div><div>Thank you very much,</div><div><br></div><div>Vanessa</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ddIXc77dBwAJ",
   "from": "Juergen Niedballa",
   "author": "0b86ca0cb4b615b0",
   "date": "2019-03-09T03:36:19Z",
   "subject": "Re: RecordTableIndividual CamtrapR question",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m glad it works and also that your workaround did the trick. The new version including the fix should be on CRAN soon.<div>Thank you for reaching out.<br></div><div>All the best,</div><div>Jürgen</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
